## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates a candidate's understanding of CGO boundary design, memory ownership semantics, and error propagation in concurrent streaming workloads.

## Key Concepts

- Memory ownership and lifetime management across language boundaries
- Safe conversion of Go slices to C pointers
- malloc/free ownership transfer and cleanup patterns
- Error handling and propagation in concurrent worker pools
- Streaming data processing with thread-safe result aggregation

## Code Example

**Header (verify_blocks.h):**
